7.    The Community Services Committee (CSC) portion of the 2026 Draft Operating and Capital Budgets:
A.    Community and Social Services Department – Children’s Services Operating Resource Requirement, “Wage Enhancement & Workforce Comp” and “Canada Wide System (CWELCC)” line items (Page 10 of the CSC Budget Book);
Carried.
B.    Recreation, Cultural and Facilities Services – Complexes, Aquatics and Specialized Services Operating Budget and User Fees (pages 34-37 of the CSC Budget Book);

WHEREAS the City of Ottawa provides residents with multiple payment options for municipal services, such as property tax payments and water bill payments, including:
AND WHEREAS the City of Ottawa has a user fees policy to recover costs associated with the delivery of public-facing services where users can be identified, as per the City’s policy and Section 391 of the Municipal Act, 2001, which provides municipalities with the authority to establish and collect user fees and charges to recover costs associated with providing a specific service;
AND WHEREAS this authority is supplemented by specific legislation, including the Building Code Act, 1992 and the Planning Act, 1990, and further supported by the City’s Fiscal Framework, which states that users of municipal services that do not benefit the community as a whole should bear some responsibility towards the costs of those services;
AND WHEREAS Service Review Working Group (SRWG) have endorsed the comprehensive user fee analysis review in line with the user fee policy and fiscal framework, as part of the Revenue optimization and generation category;
AND WHEREAS the City strives to ensure fairness, transparency, and efficiency in its payment processing costs;
AND WHEREAS the Pre-Authorized Debit fee approved by Council in April of 2025, includes an administrative cost recovery fee of $0.55 per transaction;
AND WHEREAS the City has continued improve administrative task and reduce cost pressures without increasing the resource requirement, primarily through continuous improvement and automation to keep costs low.
